<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.developer.applesignin</key>
	<array>
		<string>Default</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.developer.in-app-payments</key>
	<array>
		<string>merchant.com.mailrooms.app</string>
	</array>
	<!--
		Universal Links — DRAFTED but DISABLED for build 40.

		AASA file is live at
		  https://mailroomclub.vercel.app/.well-known/apple-app-site-association
		(verified 200 + application/json on 2026-05-15). Web fallback at
		  https://mailroomclub.vercel.app/claim?t=<token>
		works for every platform regardless of this entitlement state —
		that's how build 40 ships a usable claim flow without depending
		on the developer-portal capability flip.

		WHY DISABLED: build 40 archive attempt with this entitlement
		ENABLED failed with:
		  "Provisioning profile 'iOS Team Provisioning Profile:
		   com.mailrooms.app' doesn't include the Associated Domains
		   capability."
		Enabling here requires the App ID at
		https://developer.apple.com/account/Identifiers/com.mailrooms.app
		to have "Associated Domains" capability checked. Automatic
		signing CAN'T auto-toggle that capability in some account
		configurations.

		TO ENABLE (build 41):
		  1. Sign in at developer.apple.com → Identifiers → tap
		     com.mailrooms.app → Capabilities tab → check
		     "Associated Domains" → save.
		  2. In Xcode, Mailroom target → Signing & Capabilities →
		     "Try Again" on the provisioning profile error (or just
		     run xcodebuild archive — automatic signing will fetch the
		     refreshed profile).
		  3. Uncomment the array below.
		  4. Build 41 — Universal Links route claim taps into the
		     installed app via expo-router's /claim?t=X deep link.

		Same gating applies to the App Clip target (build 41+, after
		registering com.mailrooms.app.Clip bundle ID).
	-->
	<!--
	<key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
	<array>
		<string>applinks:mailroomclub.vercel.app</string>
	</array>
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
